The original project provided a minimal xdg-desktop-portal ScreenCast client
that paints PipeWire frames into an X11 window.  wayland-share-bridge keeps
that idea and extends it with cursor modes, persistent restore tokens,
additional pixel formats, window rules for the Hyprland compositor, a
launcher, and documentation.

Changes from the original (summary):

  - new command line interface (--cursor, --remember, --show, --title,
    --token-file, --help, --version);
  - restore token handling (persist_mode / restore_token) and a state file;
  - support for BGRx, BGRA, RGBx and RGBA frames, with channel swapping;
  - proper stride and partial-frame handling;
  - XFixes click-through input region, WM_CLASS, window type and opacity
    hints so that the mirror window can stay invisible;
  - launcher that installs Hyprland window rules (Lua and legacy parsers);
  - documentation (English and Chinese), troubleshooting and scenarios.
